TITLE: MECH-READY-QUERY's closure walk can reuse cycle-check's graph builder

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-READY-QUERY-GRAPH-REUSE
TITLE: MECH-READY-QUERY's closure walk can reuse cycle-check's graph builder
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
dev/scripts/cycle-check.py builds a UID -> [(target_uid, role)] adjacency map
over every Parent-type relation via sdoc_fp.build_uid_index and a small
RELATIONS walk. MECH-READY-QUERY needs the same shape of graph to walk a
slice's transitive contract-dependency closure and test each node's DEPTH /
STATUS against readiness. Building it should be factored into sdoc_fp.py (or
a shared graph module) once MECH-READY-QUERY is implemented, rather than
reimplemented.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Noticed while implementing SLICE-GRAPH-CHECKS: MECH-CYCLE-CHECK and
MECH-READY-QUERY both start from "walk the relation graph from a node," and
cycle-check.py already has a tested version of that walk (verified against
synthetic fixtures, see MECH-CYCLE-CHECK's NOTES). Not acted on now --
MECH-READY-QUERY is still needs-design and this is an implementation detail
for whoever designs it, not a reason to touch it while implementing an
unrelated slice.
<<<
